# reverse.list — vsock_test IDs to run in the reverse direction
# (Windows = vsock acceptor / --mode=server, Linux = vsock connector / --mode=client).
#
# Row format: see forward.list.
# Contract: every enabled (id, variant) row MUST pass — failure is a regression.
# Rows are kept in numeric-ID order.
#
# --- Reverse-direction inclusion policy ---
#
# In reverse the Windows guest is the acceptor.  After the multiple-
# pending-accepts refactor (vhi-8.1, 2026-09-10) the server-side accept
# path is a real driver-side variation, not a thin `accept + trivial +
# close` cover — every accepted socket goes through the pending-accept
# queue, the create-from-parent EA handshake, and the child socket state
# machine.  We therefore enable every `.run_server` row that reaches the
# accept path (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 12, 14, 21, 22, 24, 31), so the accept
# refactor gets exercised across the whole server-side surface.
#
# Rows still disabled in reverse are either NULL server bodies (SEQPACKET
# — see per-row notes for which of the 10 SEQPACKET ids have shared
# bodies ready in vsock_test.c vs. need upstream copy — or Linux-only),
# duplicative sequential-accept coverage already handled by test 22
# (see 18), or acceptor-side symptoms that pre-date and are orthogonal
# to the accept refactor (30 acceptor-RST-on-retry, 32 SO_LINGER not
# honoured on unread close).
#
# --- Variant coverage ---
#
# `variant` selects the Windows-side sock_ops table: `posix` (compat.h
# CRT wrappers), `wsa` (WSASend/WSARecv with 2-buf split, WSAConnect,
# WSAAccept), `overlapped` (WSA* with overlapped completion — send via
# APC, recv via event). The server body calls the same variant-dispatched
# `recv`/`send`/`accept`/`connect`, so all three flavours reach distinct
# LSP + driver paths regardless of direction. Every enabled row runs all
# three variants; if one variant fails, comment that specific line with
# a `disabled: <reason>` note rather than dropping the whole id.
# `posix-fs` / `overlapped-fs` (--io=file: CRT _read/_write resp.
# ReadFile/WriteFile on the socket handle, the driver's EvtIoRead /
# EvtIoWrite) are enabled only for the ids that reach a distinct
# read/write path, not for every row.
#
# --- Baseline ---
#
# Current baseline: vhi-8.1 HEAD 73790a30 (accept refactor + accept-on-
# non-listening WSAEINVAL fix).  Only rows known to pass on that baseline
# are enabled here.

0    posix  SOCK_STREAM connection reset
0    wsa    SOCK_STREAM connection reset
0    overlapped SOCK_STREAM connection reset
0    posix-fs SOCK_STREAM connection reset
0    overlapped-fs SOCK_STREAM connection reset
